## Oral screening requirements
The oral screening must include all of the following:

- **Early caries screening** and detection of notable findings/obvious pathology of hard and soft tissues in the oral cavity, **using a dental mirror and directed light**;
- **Counseling and educational materials** on good oral hygiene practices and nutrition for children;
- **Prescribing a fluoride supplement, if indicated**, per American Academy of Pediatrics guidelines;
- **Application of fluoride varnish** to all erupted primary teeth, beginning at tooth eruption until age 3½.

The beneficiary’s health record must document:

- **an oral evaluation and any notable findings**;
- **preventive oral health and dietary counseling with the primary caregiver**;
- **application of fluoride varnish**; and
- **referral to a dentist, if appropriate**.

Source: [Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), § 7.2.

